  "source_notes": "Compiled for the 2025-26 NCAA Division II academic year (current as of June 2026). Per task spec, ALL full member institutions of every D2 conference are listed regardless of whether the school actually sponsors tennis; the men's and women's files are identical full memberships (only the 'gender' field differs). Sources: Wikipedia 'List of NCAA Division II institutions' and individual conference pages (en.wikipedia.org); NCAA.com; conference official sites; inkblotsports.com D2 2025-26 conference rosters. autobid=true for all 23 conferences (each crowns a champion). Notable points/uncertainties: (1) 23 full D2 conferences covered. (2) Gulf South includes West Florida, which departs for D1/ASUN after 2025-26. (3) PacWest shows 13 full members for 2025-26 (Academy of Art dropped athletics after 2024-25; Menlo is in provisional/full transition). (4) CIAA reflects removal of Saint Augustine's beginning 2025-26. (5) Peach Belt includes Middle Georgia State (joined 2025-26) and Flagler (leaves for Sunshine State after 2026-27). (6) SIAC includes Tuskegee; Spring Hill leaves for Gulf South after 2026-27. (7) NSIC includes University of Jamestown (joined 2025). (8) PennWest campuses (California, Clarion, Edinboro) and Commonwealth University campuses (Bloomsburg, Lock Haven, Mansfield) are listed as separate PSAC members per their athletic branding. (9) Display names cleaned for consistency; Lincoln University appears in both GLVC (MO) and CIAA (PA) and is disambiguated.",
